{"id":"ENEE408I","title":"Capstone Design Project: Autonomous Control of Interacting Robots","department":"Electrical & Computer Engineering","level":"Undergrad","credits":"3","description":"Prerequisite: Minimum grade of C- in ENEE322. Co-requisite: ENEE460 is recommended.\n\nThe course involves students in the design,development, and application of autonomous robotic systems.The robots are 4 wheeled vehicles with on-board sensors (cameras, acoustic sensors),computers and wireless communications capabilities. The students work in teams to program the the robots to accomplish a task individually and in teams of 2 or more robots. Applications vary from semester to semester, including racing with passing, soccer, search and identify.","gradingMethods":null,"noLongerOffered":false,"removedTerm":null,"removedDetected":null,"terms":[{"term":"201801","sections":2,"seats":42,"openSeats":0,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Gilmer Blankenship"],"removed":false},{"term":"201808","sections":1,"seats":15,"openSeats":0,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Gilmer Blankenship"],"removed":false},{"term":"201908","sections":1,"seats":15,"openSeats":2,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Gilmer Blankenship"],"removed":false},{"term":"202001","sections":1,"seats":19,"openSeats":0,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Gilmer Blankenship"],"removed":false},{"term":"202008","sections":1,"seats":15,"openSeats":0,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Gilmer Blankenship"],"removed":false},{"term":"202101","sections":1,"seats":15,"openSeats":0,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Gilmer Blankenship"],"removed":false},{"term":"202108","sections":1,"seats":15,"openSeats":0,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Gilmer Blankenship"],"removed":false},{"term":"202201","sections":1,"seats":18,"openSeats":0,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Gilmer Blankenship"],"removed":false},{"term":"202208","sections":1,"seats":15,"openSeats":6,"waitlist":0,"instructors":["Shihab Shamma"],"removed":false},{"term":"202301","sections":1,"seats":18,"openSeats":3,"waitlist":0